  "result": "Shell completion now treats `#` as an ordinary character in arguments. The completion and parser tests pass (66 passed).\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`src/click/shell_completion.py`**: `split_arg_string` sets `lex.commenters = \"\"` so shlex no longer drops everything from a `#` onward.\n- **`tests/test_shell_completion.py`**: added `test_hash_in_arg_is_not_comment`, which checks `split_arg_string(\"a b#c d\")` and `split_arg_string(\"a #b\")`, plus a completion case with `b#c` as an earlier argument. I imported `split_arg_string` for it.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: the plan said to add to an unreleased section, but none existed. I added a new `## Version 8.5.1` / `Unreleased` heading above 8.5.0 with a one-line entry. Rename or move it if you use a different versioning scheme.\n\nI haven't confirmed the new test fails on the old code. I haven't committed anything.",
